// The sibling of `no-console.grit`, for the other way a line of output gets written by hand.
// Scoped by biome.jsonc to packages/*/src/** with `packages/cli/**` excluded.
//
// In a Worker this is never the right channel. Every Worker Pithy scaffolds enables `nodejs_compat`
// (see `templates/starter/apps/api/wrangler.jsonc`), so the call resolves rather than throwing — and
// what it writes is an unstructured line with no level, no name, and no instance id, which is the same
// hole `console.log` leaves, plus a dependency on a compatibility flag to not throw outright. Reach
// for the logger; it is the only thing that produces a record anyone can query.
//
// The CLI is excluded, and that exclusion is the whole reason this is a second plugin rather than
// two more patterns inside `no-console.grit`. A CLI writes to stdout — that is its product surface,
// not a leak. Forty-odd call sites under `packages/cli/src` do it through `formatDone()`,
// `formatJsonLine()` and the helpers in `terminal/style.ts`, and `docs/CLI.md` makes `--json` on
// stdout a contract every command owes an agent driving it. Banning it there would break the thing.
//
// There are no violations to fix outside the CLI today. That is the point of adding it now: the gate
// is free while the count is zero, and it stops the first one arriving quietly in a Workflow where
// it would fail at runtime rather than in review.
// The match is the member expression rather than the call, for the reason `no-console.grit` spells
// out: a method handed off as a callback is the same accident as calling it, and matching only the
// call form lets `items.forEach(process.stdout.write)` through.
language js

or {
  `process.stdout.$method`,
  `process.stderr.$method`
} as $ref where {
  register_diagnostic(span=$ref, message="Writing to stdout is the CLI's job, and only the CLI's. In a Worker this produces an unstructured line with no level, name, or instance id, and Workers Logs cannot filter it. Reach for c.var.log in a request, or createWorkerLogger() elsewhere.")
}
